<title>NETHERLANDS: FORECAST - Dutch Nov output seen up 2.8 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Dutch Nov output seen up 2.8 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank economists polled by Reuters expect November manufacturing production figures due on Monday to show a rise of some 2.8 percent compared with the same month of 1995. Economists' forecasts are summarised below:</p>
<p>GMT--Date-Period-Indicator------------Consensus--Range-----Pvs</p>
<p> 0830 20/1 Nov    Manufac. output m/m  +1.2 pct   0.8/1.7  -0.2</p>
<p> 0830 20/1 Nov    Manufac. output y/y  +2.8 pct   2.4/3.2  +2.9</p>
<p>Forecasts contributed by: ABN AMRO, ING, Generale Bank,</p>
<p>MeesPierson, NIBStrating, Rabobank.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
